<svg viewBox="0 0 720 460" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Designing an evaluation pipeline in three steps">
  <defs>
    <marker id="ch04pl-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
      <path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z" fill="var(--ink-faint)" />
    </marker>
  </defs>

  <rect x="40" y="16" width="640" height="108" rx="10" fill="var(--bg-inset)" stroke="var(--line-strong)" />
  <text x="64" y="44" font-size="13.5" font-weight="600" fill="var(--ink)">1 · Evaluate every component, at every level</text>
  <text x="64" y="66" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">end-to-end AND each intermediate step (PDF→text, text→answer) — otherwise you can't locate failures</text>
  <text x="64" y="86" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">per TURN (each response's quality) and per TASK (did the user get the job done, and in how many turns?)</text>
  <text x="64" y="106" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">task-based matters most — but task boundaries are genuinely fuzzy</text>

  <line x1="360" y1="124" x2="360" y2="146" stroke="var(--ink-faint)" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ch04pl-arrow)" />

  <rect x="40" y="152" width="640" height="124" rx="10" fill="var(--accent-soft)" stroke="var(--accent)" />
  <text x="64" y="180" font-size="13.5" font-weight="600" fill="var(--accent-ink)">2 · Create the evaluation guideline (the hardest, most important step)</text>
  <text x="64" y="202" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">define what GOOD means (correct ≠ good — “you're a terrible fit” can be correct and useless) and what's out of scope</text>
  <text x="64" y="222" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">pick criteria (teams average ~2.3) · build scoring rubrics with worked examples · validate the rubric on humans</text>
  <text x="64" y="242" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">tie metrics to business outcomes: “80% factual consistency ⇒ automate 30% of tickets” · set the usefulness threshold</text>
  <text x="64" y="262" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">the same guideline later powers annotation and finetuning data</text>

  <line x1="360" y1="276" x2="360" y2="298" stroke="var(--ink-faint)" stroke-width="1.5" marker-end="url(#ch04pl-arrow)" />

  <rect x="40" y="304" width="640" height="108" rx="10" fill="var(--bg-inset)" stroke="var(--line-strong)" />
  <text x="64" y="332" font-size="13.5" font-weight="600" fill="var(--ink)">3 · Choose methods and data</text>
  <text x="64" y="354" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">mix methods per criterion: cheap classifier on 100% + expensive AI judge on 1% · use logprobs when available</text>
  <text x="64" y="374" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">annotate real production data · SLICE it (user tiers, lengths, known-failure sets, out-of-scope set, typos)</text>
  <text x="64" y="394" font-size="11.5" fill="var(--ink-soft)">size check via bootstrap · rough rule: detecting a 3× smaller difference needs 10× more samples</text>

  <text x="360" y="442" font-size="12" font-style="italic" text-anchor="middle" fill="var(--ink-soft)">Then evaluate the evaluator: right signals? reproducible? metrics uncorrelated enough to earn their keep? · Iterate — but log everything.</text>
</svg>
